IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hcscnt-complaints`

-- Health and Community Services Complaints Act 1998 (NT) -- worked cases for the user's and complainant's questions.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text (reprint REPH016) before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are
-- HYPOTHETICAL. Dates are `the calendar date` day month year.
--
-- Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted from an unofficial copy under
-- the NT copyright policy of 8 October 1996 and the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- a user or complainant under the Health and Community Services Complaints Act 1998 (NT)`

§§ `Short names`

`any day` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2000
`HEALTH` MEANS `a service for, or purportedly for, the benefit of a person's health`
`ADMIN` MEANS `an administrative service directly related to a health service`
`AGED` MEANS `a service specifically for aged people or their carers`
`DISAB` MEANS `a service specifically for people with a disability or their carers`
`YES BASIS` MEANS `yes: this is a basis for a complaint (s 23)`
`IF UNREASONABLE` MEANS `yes, if the provider acted unreasonably, which the Commissioner decides having regard to s 5 (s 23(1))`
`NO BASIS` MEANS `no: it is not a matter in s 23, and the Commissioner must take no further action (s 30(1)(b))`
`IN TIME` MEANS `in time: made within 2 years after the user became aware (s 30(1)(c))`
`GOOD REASONS` MEANS `late, but the Commissioner is satisfied there were good reasons, so the time limit does not apply (s 30(2))`
`TOO LATE` MEANS `too late: the Commissioner must take no further action (s 30(1)(c))`
`ON TIME` MEANS `on time, or can still be (ss 27(1), 29)`
`LATE DET` MEANS `late: no determination within 60 days after the complaint was received (s 27(1))`
`LATE NOTICE` MEANS `late: no written notice to me within 14 days after the determination (s 29)`
`GOES ON` MEANS `s 30(1)(d) to (h), (3) and (4) do not stop the complaint`
`PROVIDER ON TIME` MEANS `on time, or can still be (s 66(4))`
`PROVIDER LATE` MEANS `late: the provider commits an offence, up to 40 penalty units (s 66(4))`
`CONC` MEANS `in the conciliation`
`INV` MEANS `in an investigation`
`PROSECUTION` MEANS `a prosecution for an offence against this Act`
`BOARD` MEANS `the relevant Board's proceedings about a registered provider`
`OTHER COURT` MEANS `other proceedings before a court, tribunal or board (for example, my own claim for damages)`
`GROUND` MEANS `as a ground for, or in, the Commissioner's investigation`
`MAY BE GIVEN` MEANS `only with the Commissioner's permission, which it may give (s 40(1), (2))`
`NO 48 HOURS` MEANS `no: permission cannot be given, I did not notify the provider in writing at least 48 hours before asking (s 40(2)(d))`
`NO CONDITIONS` MEANS `no: permission cannot be given, the Commissioner is not satisfied of s 40(2)(a) to (c)`
`PRESSURE OFFENCE` MEANS `an offence: up to 85 penalty units or 2 years' imprisonment (s 93(1))`
`REPRISAL OFFENCE` MEANS `an offence: up to 85 penalty units or 2 years' imprisonment (s 94(1))`
`ISSUE` MEANS `an issue arising from complaints, of public health, safety or interest or a provider's practices (s 48(1)(c))`

§§ `s 4 -- the service, disability, user`

#ASSERT `s 4 -- is the service covered` `HEALTH` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 -- is the service covered` `ADMIN` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 -- is the service covered` `AGED` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 -- is the service covered` `DISAB` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 -- is the service covered` `HEALTH` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 -- is the service covered` `none of these` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 -- is the service covered` `none of these` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 -- is the service covered` `HEALTH` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 -- is the service covered` `HEALTH` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 4 -- do I have a disability` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 -- do I have a disability` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 -- do I have a disability` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 -- do I have a disability` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a user` `I sought, used or received the service, or it was given to me` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a user` `I only arranged the service for someone else` EQUALS FALSE

§§ `s 22 -- who may complain`

#ASSERT `s 22 -- may I make the complaint` `the user (s 22(a))` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22 -- may I make the complaint` `a parent or guardian of the user (s 22(b))` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22 -- may I make the complaint` `the user's attorney under a power of attorney (s 22(c))` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22 -- may I make the complaint` `the user's attorney under a power of attorney (s 22(c))` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22 -- may I make the complaint` `a person who has the care of the user's affairs under a law or a court order (s 22(d))` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22 -- may I make the complaint` `a representative the user chose (s 22(e)(i))` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22 -- may I make the complaint` `a representative the user chose (s 22(e)(i))` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22 -- may I make the complaint` `a person with an interest in the matter, the user being unable to choose anyone (s 22(e)(ii))` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22 -- may I make the complaint` `a person with an interest in the matter, the user being unable to choose anyone (s 22(e)(ii))` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22 -- may I make the complaint` `a provider (s 22(h))` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22 -- may I make the complaint` `someone else (s 22(j))` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22 -- may I make the complaint` `someone else (s 22(j))` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§§ `s 23 -- the basis of the complaint`

#ASSERT `s 23 -- can I complain about this` `the service, or part of it, was not necessary (s 23(1)(b))` EQUALS `YES BASIS`
#ASSERT `s 23 -- can I complain about this` `the provider did not exercise due care and skill (s 23(2)(a))` EQUALS `YES BASIS`
#ASSERT `s 23 -- can I complain about this` `my privacy or dignity was not respected (s 23(2)(c))` EQUALS `YES BASIS`
#ASSERT `s 23 -- can I complain about this` `I was not given information on the treatment or services available, in terms I understand, enough to make an informed decision (s 23(2)(d))` EQUALS `YES BASIS`
#ASSERT `s 23 -- can I complain about this` `I was not given a prognosis it would have been reasonable to give me (s 23(2)(h))` EQUALS `YES BASIS`
#ASSERT `s 23 -- can I complain about this` `the provider disregarded, or acted inconsistently with, the Code, the charter or the standards in s 5 (s 23(1)(j))` EQUALS `YES BASIS`
#ASSERT `s 23 -- can I complain about this` `an applicable organisation failed to comply with the Carers Charter (s 23(1)(k))` EQUALS `YES BASIS`
#ASSERT `s 23 -- can I complain about this` `the provider did not provide a service (s 23(1)(a))` EQUALS `IF UNREASONABLE`
#ASSERT `s 23 -- can I complain about this` `something else the provider did in providing the service (s 23(1)(c))` EQUALS `IF UNREASONABLE`
#ASSERT `s 23 -- can I complain about this` `the manner in which the provider provided the service (s 23(1)(d))` EQUALS `IF UNREASONABLE`
#ASSERT `s 23 -- can I complain about this` `the provider denied or restricted my access to my records that it held (s 23(1)(e))` EQUALS `IF UNREASONABLE`
#ASSERT `s 23 -- can I complain about this` `the provider disclosed information about me (s 23(1)(g))` EQUALS `IF UNREASONABLE`
#ASSERT `s 23 -- can I complain about this` `the provider or a manager did not take proper action on, or properly investigate, my complaint to them (s 23(1)(h))` EQUALS `IF UNREASONABLE`
#ASSERT `s 23 -- can I complain about this` `something else` EQUALS `NO BASIS`

§§ `s 24 -- received`

#ASSERT `s 24(8) -- is my complaint taken to be received` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(8) -- is my complaint taken to be received` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 24(8) -- is my complaint taken to be received` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `s 30(1)(c), (2) -- the 2-year limit`

#ASSERT `s 30(1)(c) -- by what day must I complain` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2024) EQUALS `the calendar date` 10 3 2026
-- fork F3: 29 February + 2 years is the last day of February
#ASSERT `s 30(1)(c) -- by what day must I complain` (`the calendar date` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `the calendar date` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `s 30(1)(c) -- am I in time` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2024) (`the calendar date` 9 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- the last day: exactly 2 years is not "more than 2 years"
#ASSERT `s 30(1)(c) -- am I in time` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2024) (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 30(1)(c) -- am I in time` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2024) (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 30(1)(c) -- am I in time` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2024) (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `TOO LATE`
#ASSERT `s 30(1)(c) -- am I in time` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2024) (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS `GOOD REASONS`

